this was definitely going to be a storyline?
这绝对会成为一条故事线的？

1622
01:01:12.250 --> 01:01:16.810
Can you take us on this journey, this arc of the romance?
能带我们回顾一下这段旅程、这段浪漫的弧光吗？

1623
01:01:16.810 --> 01:01:19.790
When did you find out you guys were even going to kiss in this episode?
你们是什么时候知道自己甚至会在这一集里接吻的？

1624
01:01:19.790 --> 01:01:22.150
Was it at the table read or did you know before?
是在剧本围读时，还是之前就知道了？

1625
01:01:22.490 --> 01:01:24.390
Oh, that's a good question.
噢，这是一个好问题。

1626
01:01:24.650 --> 01:01:28.470
Well, first of all, I'll say that from like minute one,
嗯，首先我要说，从差不多第一分钟开始，

1627
01:01:28.470 --> 01:01:31.890
it was something we talked about, like from shooting the pilot.
这就是我们讨论过的事情，比如从拍摄试播集开始。

1628
01:01:32.170 --> 01:01:38.330
It was kind of a push and pull of they're both in love with the paper.
这有点像是一种推拉，他们两个都深爱着这份报纸。

1629
01:01:38.710 --> 01:01:41.410
Mare is so excited to finally have a job she cares about.
梅尔终于有了一份她真正在乎的工作，她兴奋极了。

1630
01:01:41.930 --> 01:01:43.610
Ned finally has his dream job.
内德终于得到了他梦寐以求的工作。

1631
01:01:44.070 --> 01:01:47.410
And there's this little bit of tension between the two of them.
他们俩之间存在着这么一点紧张感。

1632
01:01:47.570 --> 01:01:47.670
Right.
没错。

1633
01:01:47.910 --> 01:01:51.690
So it was kind of something that constantly was talked about
所以这是大家经常讨论的一件事，

1634
01:01:51.690 --> 01:01:53.750
of like, how far do we want to go with it?
那就是我们究竟想把这关系推进到什么程度？

1635
01:01:53.930 --> 01:01:56.390
Even like little looks between them in earlier episodes.
甚至包括前面几集里他们之间的小眼神。

1636
01:01:56.390 --> 01:01:58.790
It was like, we don't want to give away too much.
当时觉得，我们不想过早透露太多。

1637
01:01:58.930 --> 01:02:01.310
And also we don't totally know where it's going.
而且我们也不是完全知道它会走向何方。

1638
01:02:02.210 --> 01:02:08.330
And another thing we talked about a lot was the fact that it's only 10 episodes in the first season.
我们讨论得很多的另一件事是，第一季只有10集。

1639
01:02:08.490 --> 01:02:11.250
And, you know, we didn't know if we're going to get another season or how many seasons we'll get.
而且，你知道，我们不知道能不能续订第二季，或者能拍多少季。

1640
01:02:11.710 --> 01:02:13.610
And what do we want to show?
我们想展现什么？

1641
01:02:13.750 --> 01:02:15.570
How far should they go in the first season?
在第一季里他们应该发展到多远？

1642
01:02:16.050 --> 01:02:24.230
So when it came to the finale, I think episode nine really informed how far their relationship came.
所以在到了大结局时，我觉得第九集真正决定了他们关系的进展程度。

1643
01:02:24.510 --> 01:02:27.750
Again, with like that road trip and them being together and spending all this time together
同样，还有那次公路旅行，他们在一起，度过了所有这些时光，

1644
01:02:27.750 --> 01:02:31.950
and getting the news at the end of the nominations of the awards.
并在最后得知了奖项提名的消息。

1645
01:02:32.110 --> 01:02:36.730
I think it was all feeling like it was like, okay, something's got to happen by this point.
我觉得当时的感觉就是，好吧，到了这个时候总得发生点什么了。

1646
01:02:36.930 --> 01:02:40.710
Like somebody needs to at least try and acknowledge this.
比如总得有人至少尝试去承认这一点。

1647
01:02:40.710 --> 01:02:50.330
And the night before we shot the scene in the hallway, it was me, Donal, Paul Lieberstein,
就在我们拍摄走廊那场戏的前一晚，我和唐纳、保罗·利伯斯坦、

1648
01:02:50.610 --> 01:02:56.490
Jeffrey Blitz, Greg and Michael in a room in one of the hotel rooms for like hours just talking about it
杰弗里·布里茨、格雷格还有迈克尔在一个酒店房间里呆了好几个小时，就在那儿讨论这件事，

1649
01:02:56.490 --> 01:03:03.890
and talking about our experiences with, you know, workplace relationships and how each of us felt.
谈论我们自己关于职场恋情的经历，以及我们各自的感受。

1650
01:03:04.350 --> 01:03:08.390
And we kind of came up with like a million different ways it could end.
我们想出了大约一百万种不同的结局方式。

1651
01:03:08.390 --> 01:03:13.470
And it was, well, let's just see, why don't we give some options so when, you know,
而且当时，嗯，我们这么看，为什么不提供一些选项呢，这样当，你知道的，

1652
01:03:13.610 --> 01:03:18.030
they finally put the whole season together, they can see if it feels right that they kiss or if it doesn't.
他们最后把整季剪辑到一起时，他们就能看出他们接吻的感觉是否对味。

1653
01:03:18.390 --> 01:03:18.490
Right.
没错。

1654
01:03:18.610 --> 01:03:24.550
But I think the idea was, just to clarify, I do think the table read scripted have a kiss in it.
但我想这个想法是，澄清一下，剧本围读时的剧本里确实包含了一个吻。

1655
01:03:25.330 --> 01:03:27.990
But yeah, so we shot it a lot of different ways.
不过是的，所以我们用了很多不同的方式拍摄。

1656
01:03:28.350 --> 01:03:34.470
But it's funny because, yeah, the version they ended up using, I think, is always felt the most right.
但有趣的是，因为，对，他们最终采用的那版，我感觉，一直都是最对的。

1657
01:03:34.470 --> 01:03:35.930
I'm glad we went for it.
我很高兴我们尝试了。

1658
01:03:36.030 --> 01:03:41.610
I think it was like something that was so scary and you're just so scared to like take the air and tension out of something like that.
我觉得这就像是一件非常吓人的事，你特别害怕会把那种气氛和张力给破坏掉。

1659
01:03:41.690 --> 01:03:43.870
But I'm happy we went for it.
但我很高兴我们去尝试了。

1660
01:03:43.990 --> 01:03:46.090
It felt kind of like a swing and it was like, you know what?
感觉有点像放手一搏，当时就在想，你知道吗？

1661
01:03:46.290 --> 01:03:46.570
Yeah.
对。

1662
01:03:47.230 --> 01:03:47.810
Why not?
为什么不呢？

1663
01:03:47.990 --> 01:03:49.010
I thought it was great.
我觉得太棒了。

1664
01:03:49.010 --> 01:03:52.090
And it felt honest, you know?
而且感觉很真实，对吧？

1665
01:03:52.090 --> 01:03:56.150
I loved that even in that moment, you see who they are to each other.
我喜欢即使在那个时刻，你也能看出他们对彼此而言意味着什么。

1666
01:03:56.390 --> 01:03:57.730
Like, Mare's like, oh, come on.
比如，梅尔就像是，噢，拜托。

1667
01:03:58.410 --> 01:03:58.810
Really?
真的吗？

1668
01:03:59.010 --> 01:04:00.550
You're just going to walk away now?
你现在就要走开吗？

1669
01:04:00.730 --> 01:04:00.970
Yeah.
对。

1670
01:04:01.250 --> 01:04:01.590
You know?
你知道吗？

1671
01:04:01.790 --> 01:04:06.390
And then Ned, true to Ned, is like, come on in and kiss the pal maker.
然后内德，不愧是内德，就像是，进来吻一下这个造友者。

1672
01:04:06.390 --> 01:04:08.150
Like, I love that line.
真的，我很喜欢那句台词。

1673
01:04:08.390 --> 01:04:11.610
How much of that was scripted versus improvised?
这里面有多少是剧本写好的，多少是即兴发挥的？

1674
01:04:11.810 --> 01:04:12.590
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

1675
01:04:12.590 --> 01:04:18.090
I think a lot of it was scripted, but we definitely, there were moments.
我想很多都是剧本里的，但我们绝对，也有一些时刻。

1676
01:04:18.210 --> 01:04:26.370
I mean, one thing I loved that was scripted was that she kind of uses the journalism elements to like just seduce him.
我是说，我喜欢的一个剧本设定是，她有点利用新闻行业的元素来诱惑他。

1677
01:04:26.690 --> 01:04:30.850
Of like, well, we should just, you know, I know how much you love verifying and researching.
比如，嗯，我们应该，你知道的，我知道你有多喜欢核实和查资料。

1678
01:04:30.850 --> 01:04:38.030
So like, maybe if I word it this way, it'll seem like I can, I think she's, it's, I don't want to say manipulative, but I think there's.
所以，也许如果我这样措辞，看起来就像我能，我觉得她，这，我不想说这是操控，但我觉得有。

1679
01:04:38.090 --> 01:04:38.530
It's playful.
这很俏皮。

1680
01:04:39.270 --> 01:04:39.650
It's sexy.
很性感。

1681
01:04:39.770 --> 01:04:40.210
Yeah.
对。

1682
01:04:40.470 --> 01:04:40.690
Right?
是吧？

1683
01:04:40.690 --> 01:04:42.870
It's like the role which they say, so.
就像他们说的那个角色，所以。

1684
01:04:43.270 --> 01:04:43.430
Yeah.
对。

1685
01:04:43.590 --> 01:04:43.890
Yeah.
对。

1686
01:04:44.030 --> 01:04:49.150
So, gosh, it's so, I'm trying to remember like what, there were definitely improvised moments.
所以，天哪，太，我努力回想，绝对有一些即兴发挥的时刻。

1687
01:04:49.270 --> 01:04:51.350
Like, I remember a few times when he'd like walk away.
比如，我记得有几次他要走开的时候。

1688
01:04:51.430 --> 01:04:52.490
I'd be like, f*** off, dude.
我会说，滚开吧，老兄。

1689
01:04:52.490 --> 01:04:56.390
And like, we'd like actually get like into a fight and we tried so many different things.
然后就像，我们真的会吵起来，我们尝试了那么多不同的方法。

1690
01:04:56.390 --> 01:05:00.070
But it was one of those nights, the night before, Donald and I were just talking about it.
但那真是些难忘的夜晚之一，就在前一天晚上，唐纳德和我还在谈论这个。

1691
01:05:00.150 --> 01:05:10.270
We say like, that was one of the most special nights ever getting to sit in a hotel room and just talk with the creators about like, love and where we think this is going.
我们说，那真的是最特别的夜晚之一，能坐在酒店房间里，和创作者们畅谈爱情以及我们认为这段关系的发展方向。

1692
01:05:10.270 --> 01:05:12.030
And what feels right.
还有什么感觉是对的。

1693
01:05:12.370 --> 01:05:15.130
And it was just such a collaborative experience.
而且这是一次非常棒的合作体验。

1694
01:05:15.610 --> 01:05:22.670
And I just remember like finishing one of the takes and Jeff Blitz coming out emotional.
我只记得完成其中一个镜头后，杰夫·布里茨激动地走了出来。

1695
01:05:22.990 --> 01:05:24.830
And he was, I love Jeff Blitz.
而且他，我太喜欢杰夫·布里茨了。

1696
01:05:25.050 --> 01:05:26.710
Oh, we love Jeff Blitz.
噢，我们都爱杰夫·布里茨。

1697
01:05:26.710 --> 01:05:28.570
Is he not heaven on earth?
他简直就是人间天使吧？

1698
01:05:28.750 --> 01:05:29.130
He is.
确实是。

1699
01:05:29.350 --> 01:05:29.630
The beSt.
最棒的。

1700
01:05:29.710 --> 01:05:29.870
Yeah.
对。

1701
01:05:30.070 --> 01:05:30.490
He's everything.
他就是全部。

1702
01:05:30.730 --> 01:05:33.930
Talk about a director that makes you feel really safe to take big chances.
说起那种能让你放心去大胆冒险的导演。

1703
01:05:34.110 --> 01:05:34.510
Yes.
没错。

1704
01:05:34.950 --> 01:05:35.190
Yeah.
对。

1705
01:05:35.550 --> 01:05:39.230
And also giving us the space to be like, the cameras are going to be far away.
而且还给我们空间，比如，摄影机会离得很远。

1706
01:05:40.210 --> 01:05:44.710
We don't want you to even think that they're there because you can't think that they're there.
我们甚至不需要去想它们在那儿，因为你根本不能去想它们在那儿。

1707
01:05:44.890 --> 01:05:45.050
Yeah.
对。

1708
01:05:45.170 --> 01:05:45.350
Right.
没错。

1709
01:05:45.350 --> 01:05:52.510
And that was also another really fun element of that scene because so much of the season, they are very aware that they're being filmed.
那也是那一场戏里另一个非常有趣的部分，因为在这一季的很大一部分时间里，他们都非常清楚自己正在被拍摄。

1710
01:05:52.670 --> 01:05:53.610
In that moment, they're not.
但在那一刻，他们没有。

1711
01:05:53.970 --> 01:05:56.210
But yeah, I just remember Jeff coming out emotional.
不过对，我只记得杰夫出来时情绪很激动。

1712
01:05:56.350 --> 01:06:01.270
It made me so, I was like, oh gosh, I feel like, okay, maybe we did something remotely.
这让我超级……我当时想，哦天哪，我觉得，好吧，也许我们多少做出了一点成果。

1713
01:06:01.610 --> 01:06:01.770
Okay.
好吧。

1714
01:06:02.110 --> 01:06:03.030
You definitely did.
你们绝对做到了。

1715
01:06:03.030 --> 01:06:14.090
And the final moment, I mean, there is a tag we'll get to, but the final moment of the actual episode is Ned being like, after the kiss, he goes, oh, s**t.
还有最后的时刻，我是说，后面还有一个彩蛋，但实际这一集的最后一个镜头是奈德在接吻后说，哦，靠。

1716
01:06:14.410 --> 01:06:17.010
And then Mary has this look to camera like, oh.
然后玛丽对着镜头露出这样一个表情，哦。

1717
01:06:19.370 --> 01:06:19.850
Yeah.
对。

1718
01:06:20.110 --> 01:06:20.550
Yeah.
对。

1719
01:06:20.550 --> 01:06:22.830
I think she's pretty pleased.
我觉得她挺满意的。

1720
01:06:24.110 --> 01:06:27.450
But yeah, we talked about that, the different ways in which to end that scene.
不过对，我们讨论过那个，结束那场戏的不同方式。

1721
01:06:27.450 --> 01:06:33.450
And some were him walking out, but I liked it ending with kind of like, where could this possibly go?
有些是他走出去，但我喜欢以那种“这接下来到底会走向何方”的方式结束。

1722
01:06:34.350 --> 01:06:35.650
Well, it was great.
嗯，真的很棒。

1723
01:06:35.750 --> 01:06:36.790
I'm excited to see where it goes.
我很兴奋想看看它会走向何方。

1724
01:06:36.970 --> 01:06:37.250
Yeah.
对。

1725
01:06:37.410 --> 01:06:37.870
Same.
我也是。

1726
01:06:38.170 --> 01:06:39.630
I can't wait for season two.
我等不及要看第二季了。

1727
01:06:39.990 --> 01:06:40.590
Thank you.
谢谢。

1728
01:06:40.870 --> 01:06:41.290
Me too.
我也是。

1729
01:06:41.650 --> 01:06:47.870
And there's a delicious tag at the end of Esmeralda making a toast at the wedding that Ned and Mary got kicked out of.
片尾还有一个超棒的彩蛋，是埃斯梅拉达在奈德和玛丽被赶出来的婚礼上祝酒。

1730
01:06:47.970 --> 01:06:48.170
Yeah.
对。

1731
01:06:48.310 --> 01:06:49.210
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1732
01:06:49.790 --> 01:06:51.350
Definitely check that out.
一定要去看一下。

1733
01:06:51.450 --> 01:06:51.910
So good.
太棒了。

1734
01:06:52.090 --> 01:06:53.230
This was so fun.
这次真的太开心了。

1735
01:06:53.470 --> 01:06:56.830
And Chelsea, I want to end with this one letter that we got.
而且切尔西，我想用我们收到的一封信来作为结尾。

1736
01:06:56.830 --> 01:07:00.610
But it's just some love from Laura in Veracruz, Mexico.
这只是来自墨西哥韦拉克鲁斯的劳拉的一些爱意。

1737
01:07:01.130 --> 01:07:02.570
She says, hello, ladies.
她说，女士们好。

1738
01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:05.290
This is not a question, but a theory I'd like to share.
这不是一个问题，而是一个我想分享的理论。

1739
01:07:05.690 --> 01:07:10.630
You know how little kids watch the same movie over and over again because it makes them feel safe?
你们知道为什么小孩子们会一遍又一遍地看同一部电影吗，因为那会让他们感到安全？

1740
01:07:10.990 --> 01:07:14.790
My theory is The Office is that movie, but for grownups, it's safe.
我的理论是，《办公室》就是那部电影，但它是给成年人看的，让人感到安全。

1741
01:07:15.030 --> 01:07:17.530
We rewatch it a lot, and it makes us feel at home.
我们看了很多遍，这让我们有家的感觉。

1742
01:07:17.770 --> 01:07:20.170
So the paper felt just like that.
所以这部剧感觉就像那样。

1743
01:07:20.450 --> 01:07:22.890
A hug to all Office fans' hearts from Greg.
格雷格给所有《办公室》粉丝的心灵送上一个拥抱。

1744
01:07:23.130 --> 01:07:25.230
It has the same safe vibe as The Office.
它有着和《办公室》一样安全的氛围。

1745
01:07:25.230 --> 01:07:31.790
And I think that scene where Ned and Mary finally kiss is Greg putting everything right into place again for us.
而且我认为奈德和玛丽终于接吻的那场戏，就是格雷格为我们把一切又重新安排妥当。

1746
01:07:31.990 --> 01:07:37.250
I never feared for something to go terribly wrong with the characters because I know Greg's got our backs.
我从未担心角色们会发生什么可怕的差错，因为我知道格雷格在罩着我们。

1747
01:07:37.590 --> 01:07:38.150
Love ya.
爱你们。

1748
01:07:38.510 --> 01:07:38.810
Bye.
拜拜。

1749
01:07:39.590 --> 01:07:40.190
Laura.
劳拉。

1750
01:07:40.850 --> 01:07:41.950
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

1751
01:07:52.070 --> 01:07:54.870
Oh my gosh.
我的天啊。

1752
01:07:54.870 --> 01:08:00.570
Right now, it's truly insane when I think about it as somebody who used to watch the show when I was growing up.
现在想来，作为一个从小看这档节目长大的人，这真的太疯狂了。

1753
01:08:00.870 --> 01:08:03.770
So it makes me really happy that it made you feel that way, Laura.
劳拉，听到它能让你有这种感觉，我真的很高兴。

1754
01:08:04.130 --> 01:08:04.450
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1755
01:08:04.710 --> 01:08:05.970
Well, you have big fans.
嗯，你有很多粉丝。

1756
01:08:06.170 --> 01:08:08.270
Two of them sitting right here with you in this room.
其中有两个就坐在你身边的这个房间里。

1757
01:08:08.450 --> 01:08:11.050
And we are super excited for season two.
而且我们对第二季超级期待。

1758
01:08:11.270 --> 01:08:11.890
Thank you.
谢谢。

1759
01:08:12.110 --> 01:08:12.770
Me too.
我也是。

1760
01:08:13.290 --> 01:08:14.590
And hopefully we'll get to chat more.
希望我们以后能聊更多。

1761
01:08:14.590 --> 01:08:19.970
Thank you for answering all of our texts as we've broken down the paper.
在我们剖析剧集时，谢谢你回复了我们所有的信息。

1762
01:08:20.270 --> 01:08:26.050
And thank you for coming in today on a Sunday on your day off to talk about the finale.
也谢谢你今天在周日你的休息日抽空过来聊聊大结局。

1763
01:08:26.330 --> 01:08:27.530
